Root cause:
The bug was caused by the failure to resolve login aliases to actual usernames during the authentication process in the Ambari LDAP authentication provider. The original code directly used the username from the authentication object without resolving it, which led to issues when users attempted to log in using aliases instead of their actual usernames. The patch fixes this by incorporating a method to resolve the login alias to the corresponding username before proceeding with the user lookup.
